# JS Code Quality (Awesome + Clickr · WordPress blocks)

Defers to `.cursorrules`, `anti-overengineering`, `anti-sycophancy`, `security-appsec`, `clickr-coding-standards`.
Stack SoT: `docs/standards/javascript.md` — apply the **naming / structure / error-handling** rules; the Next.js App Router, Supabase, and Zod sections are **reference only** (this is a `wp-scripts` plugin).
Block-specific procedure lives in the `wp-block-development` skill — read it before changing `block.json` / `save.js`.

## Mindsets
- Simplicity · readability · maintainability over premature micro-opts
- Less code = less debt; 270+ block folders means every pattern gets copied

## Naming
- **MUST** `camelCase` variables/functions, `PascalCase` components, `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` module constants
- **MUST** hooks named `useThing`; handlers `handleClick` on the definition, `onClick` on the prop
- **MUST** units in names (`timeoutMs`, `maxItems`); collections plural; booleans as questions (`isSelected`, `hasImage`)
- **MUST** block attribute names match between `block.json`, `edit.js`, `save.js`, and the PHP render callback — no near-miss spellings
- **NEVER** leave `d`, `tmp`, `obj`, `x`, or vague `data` in merged code when the domain name is known

## Gutenberg specifics
- `useBlockProps()` in `edit.js` and `useBlockProps.save()` in `save.js` — never hand-write the wrapper class
- Attribute defaults belong in `block.json`, not scattered `||` fallbacks in the component
- Keep `save.js` pure and deterministic — no `Date`, no random, no `window` reads
- Markup or attribute changes to a shipped block need a `deprecated` entry, or existing posts break
- Use `@wordpress/*` packages (`components`, `block-editor`, `i18n`, `element`) — do not import React directly
- Wrap user-facing strings in `__()` / `_x()` with the `twork-builder` text domain
- `InspectorControls` panels: group related controls, avoid 60-control walls of `ToggleControl`

## Guidelines
- Early returns over deep nesting; small pure helpers over sprawling functions
- Shared logic goes in `src/shared/` — do not duplicate a helper into a 15th block folder
- DRY only when duplication is real and stable
- **Minimal diffs** — touch only task-related sections; do not reformat or rewrite unrelated comments
- **SHOULD** handle rejected promises (`await` + `try/catch`, `.catch`, or intentional `void` with a why-comment); check `res.ok` on `fetch`; check `is_wp_error` equivalents on `apiFetch`

## Front-end scripts (`assets/js/*-init.js`)
- Guard for element existence before binding; scripts load site-wide
- Prefer a single namespaced object / IIFE over ad-hoc `window.*` sprawl
- **NEVER** stash tokens, nonces beyond their scope, or PII on `window`
- Clean up listeners/observers when the init can run twice (editor preview + front end)

## Comments
- WHY only (non-obvious intent) — no restated-code comments
- JSDoc only for non-obvious shared helpers
- Workarounds: reason + date

## Bugs found while editing
- Out-of-scope bug → short `TODO(name, date):` note OR report it in the reply — do not drive-by fix unless asked

## Reject
- Importing new libraries without need/approval
- Converting block JS into a standalone React/Next/Vite app structure
- Editing a synced block in `src/` that is not in `SKIP_BLOCKS` (see `anti-overengineering`)
- `eval` / unsafe `innerHTML` / `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with attribute data (see `security-appsec`)
